'''Season twenty''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' premiered on March 16, 2015,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.wetpaint.com/dancing-with-the-stars/articles/2015-01-14-season-20-premiere-date-announced|title=Dancing With the Stars Season 20 Premiere Date Announced|last=Martin|first=Rebecca|work=Wetpaint|date=January 14, 2015|access-date=February 15, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150214011429/http://www.wetpaint.com/dancing-with-the-stars/articles/2015-01-14-season-20-premiere-date-announced|archive-date=February 14, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> and concluded on May 19, 2015.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.buddytv.com/articles/dancing-with-the-stars/abc-sets-2015-season-finale-da-56250.aspx |title=ABC Sets 2015 Season Finale Dates for 'Scandal,' 'Once Upon a Time' and More |first=Jeff |last=Dodge |work=BuddyTV |date=April 16, 2015 |access-date=April 17, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150418004835/http://www.buddytv.com/articles/dancing-with-the-stars/abc-sets-2015-season-finale-da-56250.aspx |archive-date=April 18, 2015 |url-status=live }}</ref>

This season marked the tenth anniversary of the show. In honor of this anniversary, winners [[Rumer Willis]] and [[Valentin Chmerkovskiy]] received a special 10th Anniversary golden Mirrorball Trophy.<ref name="Celebrity Cast">{{cite web |last=Sher |first=Lauren |date=February 24, 2015 |title={{-'}}Dancing With the Stars' 2015: Season 20 Celebrity Cast Announced |url=https://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/dancing-stars-2015-season-20-celebrity-cast-announced/story?id=29166872 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150224160502/https://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/dancing-stars-2015-season-20-celebrity-cast-announced/story?id=29166872 |archive-date=February 24, 2015 |access-date=February 24, 2015 |work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]}}</ref> [[R5 (band)|R5]] singer [[Riker Lynch]] and [[Allison Holker]] finished in second place, while former soldier [[Noah Galloway]] and [[Sharna Burgess]] finished in third.

==Cast==
===Couples===
This season featured twelve celebrity contestants. Ten of the professional partners were revealed on February 11, 2015, on ''[[Good Morning America]]''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2015/02/11/dancing-with-the-stars-new-season-pros/23224931/|title={{-'}}Dancing With the Stars' new season news!|first=Ann|last=Oldenburg|date=February 11, 2015|work=USA TODAY|access-date=February 15, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150214000630/http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2015/02/11/dancing-with-the-stars-new-season-pros/23224931/|archive-date=February 14, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> Joining [[Lindsay Arnold]], [[Sasha Farber]], [[Henry Byalikov]], and [[Jenna Johnson (dancer)|Jenna Johnson]] in the troupe this season were [[Alan Bersten]], from the tenth season of ''[[So You Think You Can Dance (American season 10)|So You Think You Can Dance]]'', and Brittany Cherry. Eleven of the celebrity competitors and their professional partners were revealed on ''Good Morning America'' on February 24, 2015.<ref name="Celebrity Cast" /> Witney Carson's celebrity partner was reported to be [[Chris Soules]] from ''[[The Bachelor (American TV series)|The Bachelor]]'' on March 4, 2015; Soules was later confirmed on March 10, nearly 12 hours after [[The Bachelor (American season 19)|that show's finale]].<ref name="Soules">{{cite web|url=http://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/bachelor-chris-soules-is-the-dancing-with-the-stars-mystery-contestant-201543|title=Dancing With the Stars Mystery Contestant Revealed: It's Bachelor Chris Soules!|work=[[Us Weekly]]|last=Bentley|first=Jean|date=March 4, 2015|access-date=March 5, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150305102804/http://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/bachelor-chris-soules-is-the-dancing-with-the-stars-mystery-contestant-201543|archive-date=March 5, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/bachelor-chris-soules-joins-dancing-stars-season-20/story?id=29417051 | title='Bachelor' Chris Soules Joins 'Dancing With the Stars' Season 20 Celebrity Cast | publisher=ABC News | work=[[Good Morning America]] | date=March 10, 2015 | access-date=March 10, 2015 | author=Sher, Lauren | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150311032512/https://abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/bachelor-chris-soules-joins-dancing-stars-season-20/story?id=29417051 | archive-date=March 11, 2015 | url-status=live }}</ref>

