===Week 9: Semifinals===
Couples performed one unlearned dance, and a routine coached and styled by one of the four judges. To avoid favoritism, the judges did not score the couple they coached (their absent score is marked by an '''X''' below), so the second-round dances received a total score out of 30 instead of 40.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Jacobsen|first1=Kevin|title='Dancing With the Stars' Season 20 Cast: Len Goodman Coaching Nastia Liukin & Derek Hough This Week?|url=http://www.enstarz.com/articles/85052/20150508/dancing-with-the-stars-season-20-cast-len-goodman-coaching-nastia-liukin-derek-hough-this-week.htm|publisher=EnStarz|date=May 8, 2015|access-date=May 11, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150512124508/http://www.enstarz.com/articles/85052/20150508/dancing-with-the-stars-season-20-cast-len-goodman-coaching-nastia-liukin-derek-hough-this-week.htm|archive-date=May 12, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Field|first1=Sarah|title='Dancing With The Stars' Twist: Judges Get In On The Act|url=http://www.inquisitr.com/2074173/dancing-with-the-stars-twist-judges-get-in-on-the-act/|work=Inquisitr|date=May 8, 2015|access-date=May 11, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150510204624/http://www.inquisitr.com/2074173/dancing-with-the-stars-twist-judges-get-in-on-the-act/|archive-date=May 10, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref> Couples are listed in the order they performed.

